{"id":"mahabharata-12-316","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":316,"title":"षोडशाधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 316 · Narada teaches Shuka","summary":{"en":"As Shuka studies alone, Narada comes to him and tells him to give up possessions, to master his senses and to reach the place that is without sorrow. He teaches that one must give up both dharma and adharma and both truth and falsehood, and then give up that by which one has given them up.","kn":"ಶುಕ ಒಬ್ಬನೇ ಅಧ್ಯಯನ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಿರುವಾಗ ನಾರದ ಬಂದು ಪರಿಗ್ರಹ ತ್ಯಜಿಸಿ ಇಂದ್ರಿಯ ಜಯಿಸಿ ಶೋಕರಹಿತ ಸ್ಥಾನ ಪಡೆಯಲು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಧರ್ಮ-ಅಧರ್ಮ, ಸತ್ಯ-ಅಸತ್ಯ ಎರಡನ್ನೂ ತೊರೆದು, ಅವನ್ನು ತೊರೆದ ಸಾಧನವನ್ನೂ ತೊರೆಯಬೇಕೆಂದು ಬೋಧಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"शुक अकेले अध्ययन कर रहे थे कि नारद आकर कहते हैं कि परिग्रह त्यागो, इन्द्रियों को जीतो और शोकरहित स्थान पाओ। वे सिखाते हैं कि धर्म-अधर्म और सत्य-असत्य दोनों त्यागो, और फिर जिससे त्यागा उसे भी त्याग दो।","te":"శుకుడు ఒంటరిగా అధ్యయనం చేస్తుండగా నారదుడు వచ్చి పరిగ్రహం విడిచి, ఇంద్రియాలు జయించి శోకరహిత స్థానం పొందమని చెబుతాడు. ధర్మాధర్మాలు, సత్యాసత్యాలు రెండూ విడిచి, వాటిని విడిచిన సాధనాన్నీ విడవాలని బోధిస్తాడు.","ta":"சுகர் தனியே பயிலும்போது நாரதர் வந்து உடைமைகளைத் துறந்து புலன்களை வென்று துயரற்ற இடத்தை அடையச் சொல்கிறார். தர்மம் அதர்மம், உண்மை பொய் இரண்டையும் துறந்து, அவற்றைத் துறந்த சாதனத்தையும் துறக்க வேண்டும் என்று போதிக்கிறார்.","ml":"ശുകൻ ഒറ്റയ്ക്ക് പഠിക്കുമ്പോൾ നാരദൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ അടുത്തെത്തി, സമ്പത്ത് ഉപേക്ഷിക്കാനും ഇന്ദ്രിയങ്ങളെ വശത്താക്കാനും ദുഃഖമില്ലാത്ത സ്ഥാനത്ത് എത്താനും പറയുന്നു. ധർമ്മവും അധർമ്മവും, സത്യവും അസത്യവും ഉപേക്ഷിക്കണമെന്നും, അവ ഉപേക്ഷിച്ചതിനെയും ഉപേക്ഷിക്കണമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പഠിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.316; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एतस्मिन्नन्तरे शून्ये नारदः समुपागमत् ।\nशुकं स्वाध्यायनिरतं वेदार्थान्वक्तुमीप्सितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that interval, when the place was empty, Narada came to Shuka, who was absorbed in his Vedic study, wishing to tell him the meanings of the Vedas."}},{"n":2,"text":"देवर्षिं तु शुको दृष्ट्वा नारदं समुपस्थितम् ।\nअर्घ्यपूर्वेण विधिना वेदोक्तेनाभ्यपूजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the divine sage Narada arrived, Shuka honored him with the guest-offering and the rite prescribed in the Veda."}},{"n":3,"text":"नारदोऽथाब्रवीत्प्रीतो ब्रूहि ब्रह्मविदां वर ।\nकेन त्वां श्रेयसा तात योजयामीति हृष्टवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pleased, Narada said, \"Tell me, best of the knowers of Brahman, my son, to what good shall I gladly direct you?\""}},{"n":4,"text":"नारदस्य वचः श्रुत्वा शुकः प्रोवाच भारत ।\nअस्मिँल्लोके हितं यत्स्यात्तेन मां योक्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Narada's words, Shuka replied, Bharata, \"You should direct me to whatever is truly beneficial in this world.\""}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"तत्त्वं जिज्ञासतां पूर्वमृषीणां भावितात्मनाम् ।\nसनत्कुमारो भगवानिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Long ago, when sages of purified minds were seeking the truth, the blessed Sanatkumara spoke these words."}},{"n":6,"text":"नास्ति विद्यासमं चक्षुर्नास्ति विद्यासमं तपः ।\nनास्ति रागसमं दुःखं नास्ति त्यागसमं सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no eye like knowledge, no austerity like knowledge, no sorrow like attachment, no happiness like renunciation."}},{"n":7,"text":"निवृत्तिः कर्मणः पापात्सततं पुण्यशीलता ।\nसद्वृत्तिः समुदाचारः श्रेय एतदनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Turning from sinful action, constant virtuous habit, good conduct, and right behavior: this is the highest good."}},{"n":8,"text":"मानुष्यमसुखं प्राप्य यः सज्जति स मुह्यति ।\nनालं स दुःखमोक्षाय सङ्गो वै दुःखलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever, having gained a human birth that is full of pain, clings to it is deluded. Attachment cannot free him from sorrow; attachment is the mark of sorrow."}},{"n":9,"text":"सक्तस्य बुद्धिश्चलति मोहजालविवर्धिनी ।\nमोहजालावृतो दुःखमिह चामुत्र चाश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mind of the attached wavers, and it increases the net of delusion. Wrapped in the net of delusion, one suffers here and hereafter."}},{"n":10,"text":"सर्वोपायेन कामस्य क्रोधस्य च विनिग्रहः ।\nकार्यः श्रेयोर्थिना तौ हि श्रेयोघातार्थमुद्यतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"By every means one who seeks the good must restrain desire and anger, for they are bent on destroying the good."}},{"n":11,"text":"नित्यं क्रोधात्तपो रक्षेच्छ्रियं रक्षेत मत्सरात् ।\nविद्यां मानावमानाभ्यामात्मानं तु प्रमादतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should always guard austerity from anger, prosperity from jealousy, learning from pride and insult, and oneself from negligence."}},{"n":12,"text":"आनृशंस्यं परो धर्मः क्षमा च परमं बलम् ।\nआत्मज्ञानं परं ज्ञानं न सत्याद्विद्यते परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gentleness is the highest dharma, forgiveness the highest strength, knowledge of the Self the highest knowledge, and nothing is higher than truth."}},{"n":13,"text":"सत्यस्य वचनं श्रेयः सत्यादपि हितं भवेत् ।\nयद्भूतहितमत्यन्तमेतत्सत्यं मतं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Speaking the truth is good, but what benefits is better even than truth; what is entirely for the good of beings, that I consider truth."}},{"n":14,"text":"सर्वारम्भफलत्यागी निराशीर्निष्परिग्रहः ।\nयेन सर्वं परित्यक्तं स विद्वान्स च पण्डितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives up the fruit of all undertakings, without expectation and possessions, who has abandoned everything, is learned and wise."}},{"n":15,"text":"इन्द्रियैरिन्द्रियार्थेभ्यश्चरत्यात्मवशैरिह ।\nअसज्जमानः शान्तात्मा निर्विकारः समाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here he moves among sense objects with senses under his control, unattached, calm, unchanging, and collected."}},{"n":16,"text":"आत्मभूतैरतद्भूतः सह चैव विनैव च ।\nस विमुक्तः परं श्रेयो नचिरेणाधिगच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through the senses that are his own he is not identified with them, whether with them or without them; such a freed one soon attains the highest good."}},{"n":17,"text":"अदर्शनमसंस्पर्शस्तथासंभाषणं सदा ।\nयस्य भूतैः सह मुने स श्रेयो विन्दते परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who, sage, never sees, touches, or converses with creatures finds the highest good."}},{"n":18,"text":"न हिंस्यात्सर्वभूतानि मैत्रायणगतश्चरेत् ।\nनेदं जन्म समासाद्य वैरं कुर्वीत केनचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should harm no creature and live with a friendly attitude; having obtained this birth he should make enmity with no one."}},{"n":19,"text":"आकिंचन्यं सुसंतोषो निराशीष्ट्वमचापलम् ।\nएतदाहुः परं श्रेय आत्मज्ञस्य जितात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Owning nothing, being well content, free of expectation, and steady: these, they say, are the highest good of one who knows the Self and has conquered himself."}},{"n":20,"text":"परिग्रहं परित्यज्य भव तात जितेन्द्रियः ।\nअशोकं स्थानमातिष्ठ इह चामुत्र चाभयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give up possessions, my son, and master your senses. Take a stand in a place without sorrow, fearless here and hereafter."}},{"n":21,"text":"निरामिषा न शोचन्ति त्यजेहामिषमात्मनः ।\nपरित्यज्यामिषं सौम्य दुःखतापाद्विमोक्ष्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those without craving for gain do not grieve; abandon your craving for gain. Having abandoned it, gentle one, you will be freed from the burning of sorrow."}},{"n":22,"text":"तपोनित्येन दान्तेन मुनिना संयतात्मना ।\nअजितं जेतुकामेन भाव्यं सङ्गेष्वसङ्गिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"A sage constant in austerity, self-controlled and restrained, wishing to win what is not yet won, should be unattached among attachments."}},{"n":23,"text":"गुणसङ्गेष्वनासक्त एकचर्यारतः सदा ।\nब्राह्मणो नचिरादेव सुखमायात्यनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin unattached to the qualities and always content to live alone soon attains unsurpassed happiness."}},{"n":24,"text":"द्वंद्वारामेषु भूतेषु य एको रमते मुनिः ।\nविद्धि प्रज्ञानतृप्तं तं ज्ञानतृप्तो न शोचति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage who delights alone among beings that delight in pairs of opposites: know him satisfied with wisdom; one satisfied with knowledge does not grieve."}},{"n":25,"text":"शुभैर्लभति देवत्वं व्यामिश्रैर्जन्म मानुषम् ।\nअशुभैश्चाप्यधोजन्म कर्मभिर्लभतेऽवशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good deeds one gains godhood, by mixed deeds a human birth, and by bad deeds, helpless, a lower birth."}},{"n":26,"text":"तत्र मृत्युजरादुःखैः सततं समभिद्रुतः ।\nसंसारे पच्यते जन्तुस्तत्कथं नावबुध्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, hounded constantly by death, old age, and pain, the creature is cooked in cycling existence. How do you not understand this?"}},{"n":27,"text":"अहिते हितसंज्ञस्त्वमध्रुवे ध्रुवसंज्ञकः ।\nअनर्थे चार्थसंज्ञस्त्वं किमर्थं नावबुध्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"You think the harmful beneficial, the impermanent permanent, and the useless useful. Why do you not understand?"}},{"n":28,"text":"संवेष्ट्यमानं बहुभिर्मोहतन्तुभिरात्मजैः ।\nकोशकारवदात्मानं वेष्टयन्नावबुध्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"You wrap yourself, like a silkworm, in many threads of delusion spun from your own offspring, and you do not realize it."}},{"n":29,"text":"अलं परिग्रहेणेह दोषवान्हि परिग्रहः ।\nकृमिर्हि कोशकारस्तु बध्यते स्वपरिग्रहात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enough of possessions here; possession is faulty. The silkworm is bound by its own accumulation."}},{"n":30,"text":"पुत्रदारकुटुम्बेषु सक्ताः सीदन्ति जन्तवः ।\nसरःपङ्कार्णवे मग्ना जीर्णा वनगजा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Creatures attached to sons, wives, and household sink, like old forest elephants stuck in a lake of mud."}},{"n":31,"text":"महाजालसमाकृष्टान्स्थले मत्स्यानिवोद्धृतान् ।\nस्नेहजालसमाकृष्टान्पश्य जन्तून्सुदुःखितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See creatures, dragged along by nets of affection, in great misery, like fish pulled onto dry land by a great net."}},{"n":32,"text":"कुटुम्बं पुत्रदारं च शरीरं द्रव्यसंचयाः ।\nपारक्यमध्रुवं सर्वं किं स्वं सुकृतदुष्कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Family, sons and wives, the body, hoards of wealth: all belong to others and are impermanent. What is truly yours but good and bad deeds?"}},{"n":33,"text":"यदा सर्वं परित्यज्य गन्तव्यमवशेन ते ।\nअनर्थे किं प्रसक्तस्त्वं स्वमर्थं नानुतिष्ठसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"When you must leave everything and go, helpless, why are you absorbed in the worthless and do not pursue your own good?"}},{"n":34,"text":"अविश्रान्तमनालम्बमपाथेयमदैशिकम् ।\nतमःकान्तारमध्वानं कथमेको गमिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without rest, without support, without provisions or a guide, how will you walk alone the road through the wilderness of darkness?"}},{"n":35,"text":"न हि त्वा प्रस्थितं कश्चित्पृष्ठतोऽनुगमिष्यति ।\nसुकृतं दुष्कृतं च त्वा यास्यन्तमनुयास्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When you set out, no one will follow behind you; only your good and bad deeds will follow you as you go."}},{"n":36,"text":"विद्या कर्म च शौर्यं च ज्ञानं च बहुविस्तरम् ।\nअर्थार्थमनुसार्यन्ते सिद्धार्थस्तु विमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Learning, action, valor, and the vast extent of knowledge are pursued for the sake of wealth; but one whose aim is accomplished is freed."}},{"n":37,"text":"निबन्धनी रज्जुरेषा या ग्रामे वसतो रतिः ।\nछित्त्वैनां सुकृतो यान्ति नैनां छिन्दन्ति दुष्कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This delight of one who lives in a village is a binding rope. The virtuous cut it and go; the wicked cannot cut it."}},{"n":38,"text":"रूपकूलां मनःस्रोतां स्पर्शद्वीपां रसावहाम् ।\nगन्धपङ्कां शब्दजलां स्वर्गमार्गदुरावहाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cross the river whose banks are forms, whose current is the mind, whose islands are touch, which carries tastes, whose mud is smell and whose water is sound, hard to cross on the way to heaven,"}},{"n":39,"text":"क्षमारित्रां सत्यमयीं धर्मस्थैर्यवटाकराम् ।\nत्यागवाताध्वगां शीघ्रां बुद्धिनावा नदीं तरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"with forgiveness as oar, truth as substance, steadiness in dharma as anchor, with renunciation as wind, going swiftly, with understanding as the boat."}},{"n":40,"text":"त्यज धर्ममधर्मं च उभे सत्यानृते त्यज ।\nउभे सत्यानृते त्यक्त्वा येन त्यजसि तं त्यज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give up dharma and adharma, give up both truth and falsehood. Having given up both truth and falsehood, give up that by which you give them up."}},{"n":41,"text":"त्यज धर्ममसंकल्पादधर्मं चाप्यहिंसया ।\nउभे सत्यानृते बुद्ध्या बुद्धिं परमनिश्चयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give up dharma through absence of desire, and adharma through nonviolence; give up both truth and falsehood by understanding, and understanding through supreme certainty."}},{"n":42,"text":"अस्थिस्थूणं स्नायुयुतं मांसशोणितलेपनम् ।\nचर्मावनद्धं दुर्गन्धि पूर्णं मूत्रपुरीषयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cast off this body, a dwelling of creatures, its pillars of bone, bound by sinews, plastered with flesh and blood, wrapped in skin, foul-smelling, full of urine and feces,"}},{"n":43,"text":"जराशोकसमाविष्टं रोगायतनमातुरम् ।\nरजस्वलमनित्यं च भूतावासं समुत्सृज ॥","meaning":{"en":"beset by old age and grief, a home of disease, afflicted, impure and impermanent."}},{"n":44,"text":"इदं विश्वं जगत्सर्वमजगच्चापि यद्भवेत् ।\nमहाभूतात्मकं सर्वं महद्यत्परमाणु यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This whole universe, moving and unmoving, whatever is, is made of the great elements, large or atomic."}},{"n":45,"text":"इन्द्रियाणि च पञ्चैव तमः सत्त्वं रजस्तथा ।\nइत्येष सप्तदशको राशिरव्यक्तसंज्ञकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The five senses, and darkness, goodness, and passion: this is the mass of seventeen, called the unmanifest."}},{"n":46,"text":"सर्वैरिहेन्द्रियार्थैश्च व्यक्ताव्यक्तैर्हि संहितः ।\nपञ्चविंशक इत्येष व्यक्ताव्यक्तमयो गुणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Joined with all the sense objects, manifest and unmanifest, the twenty-fifth is this quality made of the manifest and unmanifest."}},{"n":47,"text":"एतैः सर्वैः समायुक्तः पुमानित्यभिधीयते ।\nत्रिवर्गोऽत्र सुखं दुःखं जीवितं मरणं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Joined with all these, it is called the person. Here are the three aims, pleasure and pain, life and death."}},{"n":48,"text":"य इदं वेद तत्त्वेन स वेद प्रभवाप्ययौ ।\nपाराशर्येह बोद्धव्यं ज्ञानानां यच्च किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever truly knows this knows origin and dissolution. Son of Parashara's line, whatever else is to be known among kinds of knowledge is to be understood here."}},{"n":49,"text":"इन्द्रियैर्गृह्यते यद्यत्तत्तद्व्यक्तमिति स्थितिः ।\nअव्यक्तमिति विज्ञेयं लिङ्गग्राह्यमतीन्द्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever is grasped by the senses is established as manifest; the unmanifest should be understood as what is grasped by inference and is beyond the senses."}},{"n":50,"text":"इन्द्रियैर्नियतैर्देही धाराभिरिव तर्प्यते ।\nलोके विततमात्मानं लोकं चात्मनि पश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The embodied one is nourished by the controlled senses as by streams; he sees the Self spread through the world and the world in the Self."}},{"n":51,"text":"परावरदृशः शक्तिर्ज्ञानवेलां न पश्यति ।\nपश्यतः सर्वभूतानि सर्वावस्थासु सर्वदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The power of one who sees the higher and the lower does not see the limit of knowledge, for him who sees all beings at all times in all states."}},{"n":52,"text":"ब्रह्मभूतस्य संयोगो नाशुभेनोपपद्यते ।\nज्ञानेन विविधान्क्लेशानतिवृत्तस्य मोहजान् ।\nलोके बुद्धिप्रकाशेन लोकमार्गो न रिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who has become Brahman, no contact with the inauspicious arises. For one who has passed beyond the many afflictions born of delusion through knowledge, the path of the world, lit by the light of understanding, does not fail."}},{"n":53,"text":"अनादिनिधनं जन्तुमात्मनि स्थितमव्ययम् ।\nअकर्तारममूर्तं च भगवानाह तीर्थवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blessed one who knows the sacred fords says that the creature, abiding in the Self, is beginningless and endless, imperishable, not an agent, and formless."}},{"n":54,"text":"यो जन्तुः स्वकृतैस्तैस्तैः कर्मभिर्नित्यदुःखितः ।\nस दुःखप्रतिघातार्थं हन्ति जन्तूननेकधा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The creature, constantly suffering from its own various deeds, kills creatures in many ways to ward off suffering."}},{"n":55,"text":"ततः कर्म समादत्ते पुनरन्यन्नवं बहु ।\nतप्यतेऽथ पुनस्तेन भुक्त्वापथ्यमिवातुरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then it takes up much new action again, and is again tormented by it, like a sick man after unhealthy food."}},{"n":56,"text":"अजस्रमेव मोहार्तो दुःखेषु सुखसंज्ञितः ।\nबध्यते मथ्यते चैव कर्मभिर्मन्थवत्सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ever tormented by delusion, calling suffering happiness, it is bound and churned by its deeds, as a churn is turned."}},{"n":57,"text":"ततो निवृत्तो बन्धात्स्वात्कर्मणामुदयादिह ।\nपरिभ्रमति संसारं चक्रवद्बहुवेदनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, freed from its own bondage here by the rising of deeds, it wanders in cycling existence like a wheel, suffering much."}},{"n":58,"text":"स त्वं निवृत्तबन्धस्तु निवृत्तश्चापि कर्मतः ।\nसर्ववित्सर्वजित्सिद्धो भव भावविवर्जितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, with bondage ended and free of action, become one who knows all, conquers all, and is perfected, free of existence-states."}},{"n":59,"text":"संयमेन नवं बन्धं निवर्त्य तपसो बलात् ।\nसंप्राप्ता बहवः सिद्धिमप्यबाधां सुखोदयाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many, ending new bondage by restraint and the strength of austerity, have attained perfection, unhindered and giving rise to happiness.\""}}]}]}